266
00:10:14,190 --> 00:10:17,430
and reputational risk, right, for our colleges.

267
00:10:17,430 --> 00:10:19,710
And so what we did

268
00:10:19,710 --> 00:10:22,650
was we partnered with N2N.

269
00:10:22,650 --> 00:10:24,420
We brought in our subject matter experts

270
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:27,690
from Student Services and from our IT staff.

271
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:30,270
Shout out to a couple of our staff who are in the room here.

272
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:32,340
I see Jarrick, and I see a few other folks

273
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,650
who worked heavily on this project.

274
00:10:34,650 --> 00:10:37,200
And we said, "Okay, if we're gonna use AI,

275
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,870
what's the number-one thing we can do to train the model?

276
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,850
Let's use some historical data."

277
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:44,820
So we fed it a couple of years' worth of historical data

278
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,680
to be able to understand what some

279
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,030
of the patterns looked like.

280
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:50,100
We validated that with our staff

281
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,660
because they were on the front lines

282
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:54,030
and seeing on a daily basis

283
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:57,600
what the changing tactics were that were coming in.

284
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,420
And so as a result,

285
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:01,740
we got to a place

286
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:03,390
where we felt confident

287
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:05,220
that we could run this behind the scenes

288
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,710
for our fall registration last year.

289
00:11:07,710 --> 00:11:08,850
We ran it side by side

290
00:11:08,850 --> 00:11:12,540
with our in-house-developed legacy fraud model

291
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:16,380
and we actually discovered double the amount

292
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,910
of what we thought we had.

293
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:19,560
So that's the power of AI, being able

294
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:22,740
to look across these data sets and find these patterns.

295
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:26,227
So, through the collaboration, my friend Joel here said,

296
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:28,653
"You know what? We'll take that.

297
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:31,620
Right? And we'll test it."

298
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,530
And so we began this multi-district collaboration.

299
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:36,810
And then we had Santiago Canyon come on board,

300
00:11:36,810 --> 00:11:38,700
and some other districts as well,

301
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:41,250
because there was this sort of quiet network

302
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:43,380
of all of us trying to share solutions.

303
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:46,200
So I think the story is, you know,

304
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,910
working with existing partners

305
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:51,240
if they have capabilities you can quickly leverage,

306
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:55,470
being able to move quickly

307
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:57,840
in a way that's thoughtful and careful

308
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,610
but with other partnerships.

309
00:11:59,610 --> 00:12:02,700
We've benefited so much from knowing

310
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,710
that your district was seeing the same types

311
00:12:04,710 --> 00:12:06,360
of results that we were seeing

312
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:08,130
and that others that came on afterward...

313
00:12:08,130 --> 00:12:11,730
Like, it just continues to validate and improve the model.

314
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:15,090
And so today, we have, I believe,

315
00:12:15,090 --> 00:12:17,070
83 colleges now in our system

316
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,963
that are using this solution,

317
00:12:18,963 --> 00:12:20,493
the LightLeap solution.

318
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:23,260
It's just...

319
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,260
Like, sometimes, you find something that works,

320
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,670
and you go with it.

321
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:29,133
And so we've been really excited about that.

322
00:12:30,037 --> 00:12:32,280
And so again, the cross-district piece is

323
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,950
critically important, and I just wanted to share that

324
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:36,183
as part of our journey.

325
00:12:37,110 --> 00:12:38,610
- Thank you.

