00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,653
So, typical problem, right?

397
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:35,400
We have college administrators and staff

398
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,960
struggling with our platforms,

399
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:39,030
like Banner and others, right,

400
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:42,630
so developing shadow IT processes

401
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:46,050
because the existing platforms don't work.

402
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,310
So what we wanted to do

403
00:15:47,310 --> 00:15:51,480
was create a single pane of glass for these staff, right,

404
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,070
just the cognitive load

405
00:15:53,070 --> 00:15:54,900
of having to go to Argos and Banner

406
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:57,690
and gather all this information.

407
00:15:57,690 --> 00:16:00,240
Before they even talk to a student, they're exhausted

408
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:02,790
from just having to gather the data,

409
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:05,100
so the first piece was working with N2N

410
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:08,760
to develop a dashboard with all the data they need.

411
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,530
Then the second part was...

412
00:16:10,530 --> 00:16:14,220
Okay, all these programs have key eligibility

413
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,477
to see if they're qualified or not.

414
00:16:15,477 --> 00:16:17,010
And so we trained AI

415
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:20,130
to assess student data

416
00:16:20,130 --> 00:16:21,930
and determine whether they're eligible,

417
00:16:21,930 --> 00:16:23,760
so for TRIO,

418
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,490
they have to be a first-gen college student, right?

419
00:16:26,490 --> 00:16:28,170
They have to be a STEM major.

420
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:30,540
We train the model on each one of these programs,

421
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,940
so now it can go through the student data

422
00:16:32,940 --> 00:16:35,107
and determine and make an assessment:

423
00:16:35,107 --> 00:16:37,950
"Is the student qualified or not qualified?"

424
00:16:37,950 --> 00:16:39,870
And then let the advisors know,

425
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:43,200
and they can do the human assessment, right, verify.

426
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:48,200
And we flag those parts of any student's data that shows

427
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:51,240
that they're not qualified, they're not met, right?

428
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:54,000
So, great success there.

429
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,220
It goes through all kinds of student data,

