00:54:43,920 --> 00:54:45,630
And I find that those...

1307
00:54:45,630 --> 00:54:48,810
Like, pay attention to those conversations, right?

1308
00:54:48,810 --> 00:54:51,870
Because that's where the real nuggets come from

1309
00:54:51,870 --> 00:54:53,190
as folks start thinking about that

1310
00:54:53,190 --> 00:54:54,833
and coming forward with those ideas.

1311
00:54:56,790 --> 00:54:57,817
- Yeah, I would add to that.

1312
00:54:57,817 --> 00:55:01,680
You know, it's a very intentional change management process

1313
00:55:01,680 --> 00:55:02,607
when you're working with staff.

1314
00:55:02,607 --> 00:55:05,970
And so I think the thing that was most effective for me

1315
00:55:05,970 --> 00:55:09,600
was meeting with each stakeholder individually

1316
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:12,360
and giving them that time and attention,

1317
00:55:12,360 --> 00:55:15,390
being really curious about their existing process,

1318
00:55:15,390 --> 00:55:18,270
and showing respect for that process, right,

1319
00:55:18,270 --> 00:55:20,493
'cause you're asking them to let go of it.

1320
00:55:21,510 --> 00:55:23,790
So I think, you know, showing respect for that process

1321
00:55:23,790 --> 00:55:27,450
and really using that individual one-on-one space

1322
00:55:27,450 --> 00:55:28,680
to get their buy-in

1323
00:55:28,680 --> 00:55:31,710
and really sell them on the vision for what's coming,

1324
00:55:31,710 --> 00:55:33,960
because I think it can be hard

1325
00:55:33,960 --> 00:55:36,270
to go into a meeting with a bunch of people

1326
00:55:36,270 --> 00:55:37,807
and share this vision and some people are like,

1327
00:55:37,807 --> 00:55:39,750
"I don't get it. I don't see it.

1328
00:55:39,750 --> 00:55:41,010
I don't understand. But what if...

1329
00:55:41,010 --> 00:55:42,930
I'm doing this now. And how's that gonna work?

1330
00:55:42,930 --> 00:55:44,730
And they didn't think of this."

1331
00:55:44,730 --> 00:55:47,610
So starting with those individual conversations

1332
00:55:47,610 --> 00:55:49,590
and really getting everyone on board

1333
00:55:49,590 --> 00:55:51,750
and showing them kind of what our vision was

1334
00:55:51,750 --> 00:55:53,970
and, you know, expressing our commitment

1335
00:55:53,970 --> 00:55:56,610
to being very collaborative and iterative with that process

1336
00:55:56,610 --> 00:55:58,830
and making sure that their needs are gonna get met

1337
00:55:58,830 --> 00:56:01,290
and we're not gonna leave anything behind,

1338
00:56:01,290 --> 00:56:02,940
I think, really helped us have a lot

1339
00:56:02,940 --> 00:56:04,950
of buy-in, support, and enthusiasm

1340
00:56:04,950 --> 00:56:07,700
from all of the stakeholders that we were working with.

1341
00:56:09,660 --> 00:56:11,940
- Yeah, and then from my experience,

1342
00:56:11,940 --> 00:56:16,740
I think choosing partners within the college or district

1343
00:56:16,740 --> 00:56:18,840
that, you know, will show up to the project,

1344
00:56:18,840 --> 00:56:20,550
that are engaged in their own work,

1345
00:56:20,550 --> 00:56:23,133
and that like to problem-solve.

1346
00:56:24,090 --> 00:56:25,950
And then the other piece is...

1347
00:56:25,950 --> 00:56:30,950
I'd say utilize the people on this panel. Like, it comes...

1348
00:56:31,140 --> 00:56:33,570
In terms of, you know, selling an idea

1349
00:56:33,570 --> 00:56:35,580
to folks on your campus,

1350
00:56:35,580 --> 00:56:38,790
if it comes from other leaders on campuses,

1351
00:56:38,790 --> 00:56:41,070
it may get buy-in

1352
00:56:41,070 --> 00:56:43,020
better than, say, coming from a vendor.

1353
00:56:46,350 --> 00:56:50,160
- I think, for us, it's working in small groups.

1354
00:56:50,160 --> 00:56:52,773
I think smaller groups can get a lot more work done.

1355
00:56:53,700 --> 00:56:55,560
And it sounds cliche,

1356
00:56:55,560 --> 00:56:57,393
but I think, sometimes, the hardest step is really

1357
00:56:57,393 --> 00:56:59,160
just that first step.

1358
00:56:59,160 --> 00:57:01,593
And now that we've gone live,

1359
00:57:03,720 --> 00:57:08,130
again, I think that kinda eased in some of the fears

1360
00:57:08,130 --> 00:57:10,143
that we had, or staff, right?

1361
00:57:11,190 --> 00:57:12,780
I think I always encourage my staff,

1362
00:57:12,780 --> 00:57:14,730
like, "Are we making decisions out of fear?

1363
00:57:14,730 --> 00:57:17,430
Or are we making decisions of the unknown?

1364
00:57:17,430 --> 00:57:20,040
And is the unknown fear? And why is that?"

1365
00:57:20,040 --> 00:57:21,947
And so I think...

1366
00:57:21,947 --> 00:57:24,000
Again, having daily check-ins

1367
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:25,950
with the staff and also with our partners...

1368
00:57:25,950 --> 00:57:28,680
I think having really good communication with partners

1369
00:57:28,680 --> 00:57:31,620
is something that's been really reassuring for us.

1370
00:57:31,620 --> 00:57:33,870
I'm not a tech or a AI person at all,

1371
00:57:33,870 --> 00:57:35,640
and having them kinda explain things to me

1372
00:57:35,640 --> 00:57:37,440
in layman terms...

1373
00:57:37,440 --> 00:57:40,163
That's been really, really helpful for me and my staff, so.

1374
00:57:42,210 --> 00:57:43,043
- I'll keep mine brief.

1375
00:57:43,043 --> 00:57:46,110
I know you all are getting antsy for lunch.

1376
00:57:46,110 --> 00:57:47,190
My stomach's grumbling, too,

1377
00:57:47,190 --> 00:57:51,093
so I'll say, as a counselor, for me,

1378
00:57:52,650 --> 00:57:54,300
going back to the why

1379
00:57:54,300 --> 00:57:58,620
of is this going to support students and their experience

1380
00:57:58,620 --> 00:57:59,910
in a positive way,

1381
00:57:59,910 --> 00:58:01,413
if that answer is yes,

1382
00:58:02,760 --> 00:58:04,530
then that's what you need, right?

1383
00:58:04,530 --> 00:58:05,550
Like, that's the motivation,

1384
00:58:05,550 --> 00:58:07,350
and we all know that, right?

1385
00:58:07,350 --> 00:58:08,700
We're here to serve our students,

1386
00:58:08,700 --> 00:58:10,830
and if there's something within our institutions

1387
00:58:10,830 --> 00:58:12,390
that makes things more difficult for them

1388
00:58:12,390 --> 00:58:15,300
to be successful or to be able to get what it is

1389
00:58:15,300 --> 00:58:18,540
that they earned and deserve, in my case,

1390
00:58:18,540 --> 00:58:20,970
how can we take away some of those hurdles, right?

1391
00:58:20,970 --> 00:58:22,140
And everything that we've talked about

1392
00:58:22,140 --> 00:58:23,850
and all of our different programs are all different,

1393
00:58:23,850 --> 00:58:26,130
but they're all about breaking those barriers.

1394
00:58:26,130 --> 00:58:28,230
And so if that serves the student experience

1395
00:58:28,230 --> 00:58:29,130
in a positive way,

1396
00:58:29,130 --> 00:58:31,380
like, pff, you have all...

1397
00:58:31,380 --> 00:58:32,910
All of that is always gonna serve you

1398
00:58:32,910 --> 00:58:34,533
in completing your goals.

1399
00:58:36,210 --> 00:58:37,830
- Well, I wanna thank all of the panelists.

1400
00:58:37,830 --> 00:58:40,320
Thank you so much for sharing about what you're doing

1401
00:58:40,320 --> 00:58:43,983
at your institution. (audience applauds)

1402
00:58:45,748 --> 00:58:48,193
Thank you to our leaders and our audience here.

1403
00:58:48,193 --> 00:58:50,940
I hope that this has sparked some ideas for you

1404
00:58:50,940 --> 00:58:53,250
and you have some takeaways of maybe where you're going

1405
00:58:53,250 --> 00:58:56,100
to engage in some dialogue at your institutions.

1406
00:58:56,100 --> 00:58:59,850
And you have some resources up here if you need some help.

1407
00:58:59,850 --> 00:59:02,130
Sorry for volunteering you. (laughs)

